node_modules
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-store
# Credentials. `.env` and `config.json` were the only protected names, so `.env.local`, `config.local.json` and a
# private key dropped in the tree were one `git add -A` away from being committed
.env
.env.*
config.json
config.*.json
!config.json.example
*.pem
*.key
# The same credential class `.dockerignore` keeps out of the image, ignored here so `git add -A` cannot commit it in
# the first place: package-manager and git credential files (`.npmrc` is where a registry token lives), an SSH private
# key and a PKCS#12/keystore bundle.
.npmrc
.pnpmrc
.yarnrc
.yarnrc.yml
.netrc
_netrc
.git-credentials
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
# Editor and IDE state: not a credential, but it is machine-local and never belongs in a commit
.vscode
.idea
